                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "922dd04e-9fe3-3683-b78b-7f137e2bf99d",
                        "entry_id": "251f89ef-3c87-3d28-8acf-449973302bc3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Bösewicht in Märchen, menschenfressendes Ungeheuer"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a07357c-0c9a-4a99-af10-1aa397a9d417",
                                "sense_id": "922dd04e-9fe3-3683-b78b-7f137e2bf99d",
                                "text": "Die Oger führen im Kampf meist Waffen und ernähren sich allzugern vom Fleisch der Menschen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1fb67e8-2c12-4fb3-9639-f3dcc902858a",
                                "sense_id": "922dd04e-9fe3-3683-b78b-7f137e2bf99d",
                                "text": "In dem Märchen vom Kleinen Däumling kommt ein Oger vor."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d54d207e-d02e-3a65-b38a-632a49519856",
                        "entry_id": "251f89ef-3c87-3d28-8acf-449973302bc3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "menschenähnliches, jedoch abscheulich aussehende Kreatur, die von immenser Kraft und Körpergröße zeugt und meist mit Keulen oder Ähnlichem kämpft"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "heute"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "43f5298a-68cd-429b-8134-c4f5bf8fb398",
                                "sense_id": "d54d207e-d02e-3a65-b38a-632a49519856",
                                "text": "Shrek ist ein Film über einen giftgrünen, häßlichen Oger mit schottischem Akzent."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c41c38a4-8a3e-4908-8dba-277313e1b6a1",
                        "source_entry_id": "251f89ef-3c87-3d28-8acf-449973302bc3",
                        "source_sense_id": "922dd04e-9fe3-3683-b78b-7f137e2bf99d",
                        "source_sense_description": "Bösewicht in Märchen, menschenfressendes Ungeheuer",
                        "target_lang_word": "ogre",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ogre",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d44c5720-4709-3a8f-a73a-7dff7bbca5c8",
                                        "entry_id": "4a9cbed8-9a4b-3c3f-b747-04d6656fb633",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of brutish giant from folk tales that eats human flesh."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1c9a107-03c0-4a39-b286-1cb54ff007a3",
                                                "sense_id": "d44c5720-4709-3a8f-a73a-7dff7bbca5c8",
                                                "text": "And in the seventh tale of the third day of the same collection, when Corvetto had hidden himself under the Ogre's bed to steal his quilt, \"he began to pull quite gently, when the Ogre awoke, and bid his wife not to pull the clothes that way, or she'd strip him, and he would get his death of cold.\" \"Why, it's you that are stripping me,\" replied the Ogress, \"and you have not left a stitch on me.\" \"Where the devil is the quilt?\" says the Ogre[.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b36a7cb-69fd-4b3d-95c7-e10baa94458e",
                                                "sense_id": "d44c5720-4709-3a8f-a73a-7dff7bbca5c8",
                                                "text": "And the conquest of the ogres comes at the right moment: not in earliest youth, though the nicors are referred in Beowulf's geogoðfeore as a presage of the kind of hero we have to deal with[.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d87b64cb-8d79-4488-8bdb-2b3945fcc0d6",
                                                "sense_id": "d44c5720-4709-3a8f-a73a-7dff7bbca5c8",
                                                "text": "From his end of the hall Beowulf watched the ogre, weighed his endowment, and waited to see how Grendel would strike."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b84778c-661d-3cb2-b71e-6ccb59b53176",
                                        "entry_id": "4a9cbed8-9a4b-3c3f-b747-04d6656fb633",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cruel person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ae69830-3afd-4cd1-86d0-44e90281f9a0",
                                                "sense_id": "6b84778c-661d-3cb2-b71e-6ccb59b53176",
                                                "text": "People are going to think I'm an ogre if I refuse to buy coffee for my little brother!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5d021439-e3d5-48ba-ba80-aaea2f9c1c4c",
                        "source_entry_id": "251f89ef-3c87-3d28-8acf-449973302bc3",
                        "source_sense_id": "922dd04e-9fe3-3683-b78b-7f137e2bf99d",
                        "source_sense_description": "Bösewicht in Märchen, menschenfressendes Ungeheuer",
                        "target_lang_word": "ogre",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ogre",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79b8b1cc-e718-3517-b0a8-34b7151beef8",
                                        "entry_id": "934ca3af-2657-3f76-9b54-28c4aca92a93",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personnage de conte de fées, sorte de monstre, de géant qui passe pour se nourrir de chair humaine, spécialement de celle des enfants."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Fantastique"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dda0e9dd-7484-4964-9881-7f91e6cace2f",
                                                "sense_id": "79b8b1cc-e718-3517-b0a8-34b7151beef8",
                                                "text": "[…] à un enfant turbulent : Il y a des jours où l’absence d’ogre se fait cruellement sentir."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40724a13-f860-4e15-9213-c51f88380d09",
                                                "sense_id": "79b8b1cc-e718-3517-b0a8-34b7151beef8",
                                                "text": "[…] on eût dit qu’il y avait dans cette cave un de ces ogres faméliques, gigantesques héros des légendes populaires, et dont nul ne force impunément la caverne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ea49557-cd84-3ad1-8102-13ded23f8748",
                                        "entry_id": "934ca3af-2657-3f76-9b54-28c4aca92a93",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mangeur vorace ; goinfre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f4609ee-f97b-4c00-bb04-3a4674cc5e58",
                                                "sense_id": "2ea49557-cd84-3ad1-8102-13ded23f8748",
                                                "text": "Avoir un appétit d’ogre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee58d981-fa75-36dc-9ed3-47ebeeb9a194",
                                        "entry_id": "934ca3af-2657-3f76-9b54-28c4aca92a93",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne possessive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bde4a823-05ae-4a0e-9437-5e8e2bcf3b2e",
                                                "sense_id": "ee58d981-fa75-36dc-9ed3-47ebeeb9a194",
                                                "text": "Ces ogres et ces ogresses n’ont heureusement plus de dents et en sont réduits à vous manger des yeux."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a11b5b20-dfe5-34a8-97ab-3de2d29b313c",
                                        "entry_id": "934ca3af-2657-3f76-9b54-28c4aca92a93",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Repris de justice tenancier d’un tapis-franc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6714d18-2e8f-4c66-9662-e82d65d52e5b",
                                                "sense_id": "a11b5b20-dfe5-34a8-97ab-3de2d29b313c",
                                                "text": "Un tapis-franc, en argot de vol et de meurtre, signifie un estaminet ou un cabaret du plus bas étage.\nUn repris de justice, qui, dans cette langue immonde, s’appelle un ogre, ou une femme de même dégradation, qui s’appelle une ogresse, tiennent ordinairement ces tavernes, hantées par le rebut de la population parisienne ; forçats libérés, escrocs, voleurs, assassins y abondent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
